[2026-02-04T00:23:40.221Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Keyset Pagination Eliminating Cursor Lookup\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n- **Generated**: 2/1/2026, 11:43:09 PM\n\n## Description\nReplace cursor-based pagination in sessions/route.ts:68-79 with keyset pagination that passes created_at directly from the client. Currently, each paginated request makes an extra database query just to fetch the cursor row's created_at value. Pass {lastId, lastCreatedAt} from the client, eliminating the lookup entirely. Also cache total counts separately rather than computing on every request.\n\n## Reasoning\nEvery pagination request makes 2 DB queries instead of 1, adding ~25ms latency per page. For users scrolling through session history, this doubles perceived load time. Keyset pagination is also more reliable than offset-based approaches at scale and prevents skipped/duplicate rows during concurrent writes.\n\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d184f0d2-244e-457f-8ea5-4627f2d647f1","uuid":"13542984-0cb1-42b2-9240-3c166ba269f9","isSynthetic":true}
